# Implementation Walkthrough: Domain Routing & i18n

We have successfully implemented domain-based routing and multi-language support for the Evaitec Dashboard.

## Changes Made

### 1. Localization Files
Created [tr.json](file:///c:/projects/github/casatozima/src/translations/tr.json) and [en.json](file:///c:/projects/github/casatozima/src/translations/en.json) in `src/translations/` to manage all UI text centrally.

### 2. Backend Routing (`app.py`)
- Added `before_request` hook to detect domain and geo-location.
- **Redirection Logic**:
    - `evaitec.com.tr` -> Always Turkish.
    - `evaitec.com` (from TR) -> Redirects to `evaitec.com.tr`.
    - `evaitec.com` (International) -> English (via `/en/` path).
- Supports `/en` and `/en/` routes for explicit English access.

### 3. Frontend Localization (`index.html`)
- Replaced hardcoded Turkish text with template variables.
- Added a **Language Switcher** in the header.
- Localized dynamic JavaScript feedback (toasts, loading states).

### 4. SSH & Infrastructure
- Fixed SSH access to ZimaOS using a passphrase-free key.
- Resolved ZimaOS DNS issues (`ota.zimaos.com`) by configuring `resolv.conf`.

## Verification Plan

### Domain Redirection
1. Access `evaitec.com` from a Turkish IP -> Should redirect to `evaitec.com.tr`.
2. Access `evaitec.com` from an international IP -> Should show the English dashboard.

### Language Toggle
- Click **TR** or **EN** in the header to switch languages manually.

### ZimaOS Update
- Confirm ZimaOS 1.5.4 update completed successfully.
